<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $C$ be an object of $\calC $ and let $E = p(C)$. Consider the composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\calC ^0_{E})^{\triangleright }_{/C} \stackrel{G^{\triangleright }}{\rightarrow } (\calC ^{0}_{/C})^{\triangleright } \stackrel{F_{C}}{\rightarrow } \calD . \]
</div>
    <p>
       We will show that $F_ C$ is a colimit diagram if and only if $F_ C \circ G^{\triangleright }$ is a colimit diagram. For this, it suffices to show that the inclusion $G: (\calC ^{0}_{E})_{/C} \subseteq \calC ^{0}_{/C}$ is cofinal. According to Proposition <a href="/tag/B38B7D" data-tag="B38B7D">2.4.3.3</a>, the projection $p': \calC _{/C} \rightarrow \calE _{/E}$ is a coCartesian fibration, and a morphism 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { C' \ar [rr]^{f} \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  C'' \ar [dl] \\ &amp;  C &amp;  } \]
</div>
    <p>
       in $\calC _{/C}$ is $p'$-coCartesian if and only if $f$ is $p$-coCartesian. It follows that $p'$ restricts to a coCartesian fibration $\calC '_{/C} \rightarrow \calE _{/E}$. We have a pullback diagram of simplicial sets 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { (\calC ^{0}_{E})_{/C} \ar [r]^{G} \ar [d] &amp;  \calC ^0_{/C} \ar [d] \\ \{  \id _{E} \}  \ar [r]^{G_0} &amp;  \calE _{/E}} \]
</div>
    <p>
       The right vertical map is smooth (Proposition <a href="/tag/B9BB9A" data-tag="B9BB9A">4.1.2.14</a>) and $G_0$ is right anodyne, so that $G$ is right anodyne as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>